<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>CostGuard report: {{ totals.monthly | money }}/month potential savings</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --ink: #15212b; --muted: #5a6670; --rule: #dde2e5; --bg: #f5f6f4; --panel: #ffffff;
    --save: #1d6b47; --save-bg: #e2f0e8;
    --med: #8a5800; --med-bg: #faeed3;
    --high: #a3271c; --high-bg: #f7e0dc;
    --bar-now: #b9c2c8;
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body {
    margin: 0; background: var(--bg); color: var(--ink);
    font: 15px/1.5 -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;
  }
  .wrap { max-width: 1180px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 40px 28px 64px; }
  header { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-end; gap: 24px;
           border-bottom: 2px solid var(--ink); padding-bottom: 16px; margin-bottom: 28px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  h1 { font-size: 26px; margin: 0; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  h1 small { display: block; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 400; color: var(--muted); letter-spacing: 0; margin-top: 4px; }
  .meta { font-size: 13px; color: var(--muted); text-align: right; }
  .meta b { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }
  h2 { font-size: 18px; margin: 44px 0 6px; }
  .lede { color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 16px; font-size: 14px; }

  .stats { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); border: 1px solid var(--rule); background: var(--panel); }
  .stat { padding: 18px 20px; border-right: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .stat:last-child { border-right: 0; }
  .stat .label { font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .06em; color: var(--muted); }
  .stat .value { font-size: 28px; font-weight: 650; margin-top: 4px; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .stat .sub { font-size: 13px; color: var(--muted); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .stat.key { background: var(--save-bg); }
  .stat.key .value { color: var(--save); }

  .riskbar { display: flex; height: 14px; margin: 14px 0 10px; background: var(--rule); }
  .riskbar span { display: block; height: 100%; }
  .riskbar .low, .sw.low { background: var(--save); }
  .riskbar .medium, .sw.medium { background: #d79a1e; }
  .riskbar .high, .sw.high { background: var(--high); }
  .legend { display: flex; gap: 28px; flex-wrap: wrap; font-size: 14px; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .legend i { display: inline-block; width: 10px; height: 10px; margin-right: 6px; vertical-align: 0; }

  .panel { background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--rule); overflow-x: auto; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 14px; }
  th, td { padding: 10px 10px; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  th { font-size: 12px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--muted); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .05em;
       background: #fafbfa; white-space: nowrap; }
  tbody tr:last-child td { border-bottom: 0; }
  tfoot td { border-top: 2px solid var(--ink); border-bottom: 0; font-weight: 650; }
  .num { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; white-space: nowrap; }
  .id { font-weight: 600; white-space: nowrap; }
  .id a { color: var(--ink); text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-color: #9aa5ad; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  tr.main td { border-bottom: 0; padding-bottom: 4px; }
  tr.detail td { padding-top: 0; font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--muted); }
  tr.detail b { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }
  .type { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace; font-size: 13px; white-space: nowrap; }
  .spec { display: block; color: var(--muted); font-size: 12px; }
  .arrow { color: var(--muted); padding: 0 2px; }
  .save { color: var(--save); font-weight: 600; }
  .note { color: var(--muted); font-size: 12.5px; margin-top: 3px; }

  .tag { display: inline-block; padding: 1px 7px; border-radius: 3px; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 600;
         text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .04em; white-space: nowrap; }
  .tag.low { color: var(--save); background: var(--save-bg); }
  .tag.medium { color: var(--med); background: var(--med-bg); }
  .tag.high { color: var(--high); background: var(--high-bg); }
  .tag.oversized { color: var(--high); background: var(--high-bg); }
  .tag.right_sized { color: var(--muted); background: #eceff1; }
  .tag.insufficient_data { color: var(--med); background: var(--med-bg); }

  .costbars { width: 80px; min-width: 80px; }
  .costbars div { height: 6px; margin: 3px 0; }
  .costbars .now { background: var(--bar-now); }
  .costbars .new { background: var(--save); }

  .usage { white-space: nowrap; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .dim { color: var(--muted); }
  .empty { padding: 22px; color: var(--muted); }
  ul.plain { margin: 8px 0 0; padding-left: 20px; font-size: 14px; }
  ul.plain li { margin: 4px 0; }
  .method { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 28px; font-size: 14px; }
  .method h3 { font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 6px; }
  .method p, .method ul { margin: 0 0 10px; color: var(--muted); }
  .method ul { padding-left: 18px; }
  footer { margin-top: 48px; padding-top: 14px; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--muted); }

  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .stats { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
    .stat:nth-child(2) { border-right: 0; }
    .stat:nth-child(-n+2) { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
    .method { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .meta { text-align: left; }
  }
  @media print {
    body { background: #fff; font-size: 12px; }
    .wrap { max-width: none; padding: 0; }
    .panel, .stats { border-color: #bbb; }
    tr { break-inside: avoid; }
    h2 { break-after: avoid; }
    * { -webkit-print-color-adjust: exact; print-color-adjust: exact; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">

<header>
  <h1>CostGuard: RDS right-sizing report
    <small>Over-provisioned databases and what downsizing them would save</small>
  </h1>
  <div class="meta">
    Region <b>{{ region }}</b><br>
    Usage window <b>last {{ thresholds.observation_days }} days</b><br>
    Generated <b>{{ generated_at }}</b>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="stats" aria-label="Summary">
  <div class="stat">
    <div class="label">Current spend</div>
    <div class="value">{{ spend.current_monthly | money(0) }}</div>
    <div class="sub">per month &middot; {{ spend.current_annual | money(0) }}/yr</div>
  </div>
  <div class="stat key">
    <div class="label">Potential savings</div>
    <div class="value">{{ totals.monthly | money(0) }}</div>
    <div class="sub">per month &middot; {{ totals.annual | money(0) }}/yr</div>
  </div>
  <div class="stat">
    <div class="label">Spend after changes</div>
    <div class="value">{{ spend.projected_monthly | money(0) }}</div>
    <div class="sub">per month &middot; {{ spend.savings_pct }}% lower</div>
  </div>
  <div class="stat">
    <div class="label">Databases analysed</div>
    <div class="value">{{ counts.total }}</div>
    <div class="sub">{{ counts.oversized }} over-sized &middot; {{ counts.right_sized }} right-sized &middot; {{ counts.skipped }} skipped</div>
  </div>
</section>

{% if recommendations %}
<h2>Savings by risk level</h2>
<p class="lede">Risk reflects how close the database would run to its limits on the smaller size. Low-risk changes can usually be scheduled straight away.</p>
<div class="riskbar" role="img" aria-label="Savings split by risk level">
  {% for level in risk_levels if risk[level].monthly %}
  <span class="{{ level }}" style="width: {{ risk[level].monthly | bar_width(totals.monthly) }}%"></span>
  {% endfor %}
</div>
<div class="legend">
  {% for level in risk_levels %}
  <div><i class="sw {{ level }}"></i>
    <b>{{ level | capitalize }}</b>: {{ risk[level].monthly | money }}/mo
    <span class="dim">({{ risk[level].count }} change{{ '' if risk[level].count == 1 else 's' }})</span></div>
  {% endfor %}
</div>
{% endif %}

<h2>Recommended changes</h2>
<p class="lede">Each change stays in the same instance family. Projected figures are this database's observed peaks scaled onto the smaller size.</p>
<div class="panel">
{% if recommendations %}
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Database</th><th>Change</th><th class="num">Now $/mo</th><th class="num">New $/mo</th>
        <th>Cost</th><th class="num">Save $/mo</th><th class="num">Save $/yr</th>
        <th>On new size</th><th>Risk</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
    {% for r in recommendations %}
      <tr id="rec-{{ r.instance_id }}" class="main">
        <td class="id">{{ r.instance_id }}</td>
        <td class="type">{{ r.current_type }} <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span> {{ r.recommended_type }}
          <span class="spec">{{ r.current_vcpus }} vCPU / {{ r.current_memory_gb | gb }} &rarr; {{ r.recommended_vcpus }} vCPU / {{ r.recommended_memory_gb | gb }}</span></td>
        <td class="num">{{ r.current_cost | money }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ r.recommended_cost | money }}</td>
        <td class="costbars" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="now" style="width: {{ r.current_cost | bar_width(max_cost) }}%"></div>
          <div class="new" style="width: {{ r.recommended_cost | bar_width(max_cost) }}%"></div>
        </td>
        <td class="num save">{{ r.monthly_savings | money }}<div class="note">{{ r.savings_pct }}% less</div></td>
        <td class="num save">{{ r.annual_savings | money }}</td>
        <td class="usage">CPU p95 {{ r.projected_cpu_peak_pct | pct }}
          <span class="spec">busiest minute {{ r.projected_cpu_max_pct | pct }} &middot; memory {{ r.projected_memory_peak_pct | pct }}</span></td>
        <td><span class="tag {{ r.risk_level }}">{{ r.risk_level }}</span></td>
      </tr>
      <tr class="detail">
        <td colspan="9"><b>Why:</b> {{ r.reason | plain }}. <b>Risk:</b> {{ r.risk_reason }}.</td>
      </tr>
    {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
    <tfoot>
      <tr>
        <td colspan="2">Total ({{ recommendations | length }} change{{ '' if recommendations | length == 1 else 's' }})</td>
        <td class="num">{{ recommendations | sum(attribute='current_cost') | money }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ recommendations | sum(attribute='recommended_cost') | money }}</td>
        <td></td>
        <td class="num save">{{ totals.monthly | money }}</td>
        <td class="num save">{{ totals.annual | money }}</td>
        <td colspan="2"></td>
      </tr>
    </tfoot>
  </table>
{% else %}
  <div class="empty">No downgrade recommendations. Every database with enough data is right-sized.</div>
{% endif %}
</div>

{% if no_safe_downgrade or skipped or spend.unpriced %}
<h2>Needs attention</h2>
<ul class="plain">
  {% if no_safe_downgrade %}
  <li><b>Over-sized, but no safe smaller size in the same family:</b> {{ no_safe_downgrade | join(', ') }}.
    Either it is already the smallest size, or its busiest CPU minute or memory peak would not fit on the next size down. A different instance family may help.</li>
  {% endif %}
  {% for row in skipped %}
  <li><b>{{ row.instance_id }}</b> was skipped: {{ row.reason | plain }}</li>
  {% endfor %}
  {% if spend.unpriced %}
  <li><b>No price on file</b> for {{ spend.unpriced | join(', ') }}, so current spend above is a lower bound.</li>
  {% endif %}
</ul>
{% endif %}

<h2>All databases</h2>
<p class="lede">Usage over the last {{ thresholds.observation_days }} days. CPU p95 is the 95th percentile of hourly peaks; memory peak is the lowest free memory seen.</p>
<div class="panel">
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Database</th><th>Type</th><th>Engine</th><th class="num">$/mo</th>
        <th class="num">CPU avg</th><th class="num">CPU p95</th><th class="num">CPU max</th>
        <th class="num">Mem avg</th><th class="num">Mem peak</th>
        <th class="num">Conns</th><th class="num">Storage used</th><th>Verdict</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
    {% for row in rows %}
      <tr>
        <td class="id">{% if row.has_recommendation %}<a href="#rec-{{ row.instance_id }}">{{ row.instance_id }}</a>{% else %}{{ row.instance_id }}{% endif %}</td>
        <td class="type">{{ row.instance_type }}{% if row.multi_az %}<span class="spec">Multi-AZ</span>{% endif %}</td>
        <td>{{ row.engine }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ row.monthly_cost | money if row.priced else 'unpriced' }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ row.cpu_avg_pct | pct }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ row.cpu_p95_pct | pct }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ row.cpu_max_pct | pct }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ row.memory_avg_pct | pct }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ row.memory_max_pct | pct }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ row.connections_avg if row.connections_avg is not none else 'n/a' }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ row.storage_used_gb | gb }}<span class="spec">of {{ row.storage_allocated_gb | gb }}</span></td>
        <td><span class="tag {{ row.status }}">{{ row.verdict }}</span></td>
      </tr>
    {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<h2>How decisions were made</h2>
<div class="method">
  <div>
    <h3>Over-sized when CPU and memory are both always low</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>CPU average below {{ thresholds.cpu_avg | pct }} and p95 peak below {{ thresholds.cpu_peak | pct }}</li>
      <li>Memory average below {{ thresholds.mem_avg | pct }} and peak below {{ thresholds.mem_peak | pct }}</li>
      <li>Databases with under half the expected hourly data are skipped, never reported as healthy</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Smallest size that still fits</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Projected CPU p95 at most {{ thresholds.target_cpu | pct }}, memory peak at most {{ thresholds.target_mem | pct }}</li>
      <li>The single busiest CPU minute must still fit (at most {{ thresholds.cpu_saturation | pct }})</li>
      <li>A step that only removes RAM is never taken without memory data</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div>
    <h3>Risk level</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Low</b>: projected peak at most {{ thresholds.low_risk | pct }}, with memory usage known</li>
      <li><b>Medium</b>: projected peak at most {{ thresholds.medium_risk | pct }}</li>
      <li><b>High</b>: anything above, or the busiest minute would exceed {{ thresholds.high_risk_cpu | pct }}</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Cost</h3>
    <p>On-demand compute price &times; 730 hours per month, adjusted by region and doubled for Multi-AZ. Annual savings are monthly &times; 12. Storage, IOPS, backups and Reserved Instance discounts are not included; they don't change with a downsize, so the savings figures still hold.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<footer>Generated by CostGuard. Read-only analysis: no changes were made to your AWS account. Prices are estimates, not your bill.</footer>
</div>
</body>
</html>
